<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/028W">Remark <span data-tag="028W">5.6.5.2</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a cocartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories and let $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ be a functor. By virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="0285" href="/tag/0285">5.1.7.5</a>, a diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{U} \ar [r]^-{ \widetilde{\mathscr {F}} } &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{\operatorname{Obj}} \ar [d]^{V} \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r]^-{ \mathscr {F} } &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}} \]
</div>
<p> witnesses $\mathscr {F}$ as a covariant transport representation for $U$ if and only if the induced map $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \mathscr {F}$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. We will later extend this observation to the case where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a general simplicial set (Corollary <a data-tag="029K" href="/tag/029K">5.6.7.8</a>). </p>
</article>
